   "id": "anthropic",
   "paragraph": "An AI model can be offered with different rules about who can use it and what it can help with. Think of the same workshop tool being available under different safety rules. Anthropic introduced Claude Fable 5.2 and Mythos 5.2 on November 9. They share the same underlying model but use different safeguards. Fable is broadly available across Claude platforms, while Mythos is limited to verified organisations in cybersecurity and biomedical research. Anthropic says the new models are up to 30% faster than the previous 5.1 generation. Actual speed depends on the task, and the speed claim leaves open how reliably the models perform in those fields.",
   "headline": "Anthropic gives one model two sets of safeguards",
   "facts": [
    "Announced 9 Nov",
    "Claude Fable 5.2 and Mythos 5.2 share an underlying model with different safeguards",
    "Fable broadly available across Claude platforms; Mythos restricted to verified organisations in cybersecurity and biomedical research",
    "Company says up to 30% faster versus 5.1; workload performance and broader reliability are open questions"
